/audit.orm-entity.ts\",\n    \"libs/platform/database/src/migrations/1722540000000-CreateIdentityAccessSchema.ts\",\n    \"libs/platform/database/src/migrations/1722550000000-CreateUserProfilesSchema.ts\",\n    \"libs/platform/database/src/public-api.ts\",\n    \"libs/platform/security/src/**\",\n    \"libs/shared/kernel/src/entities/auditable-props.ts\",\n    \"libs/shared/kernel/src/public-api.ts\",\n    \"nest-cli.json\",\n    \"package.json\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\"\n  ],\n  \"decisions\": [\n    \"Resolved fix-request-review-1.md item 9 (missing deterministic validation) by running lint, typecheck, unit test, build, test:architecture, migration:run+revert on a disposable empty database, and test:e2e against the real docker-compose test stack (postgres/redis/minio); all passed in this cycle.\",\n    \"Items 1-8 of fix-request-review-1.md were already implemented in the worktree carried over from implementation cycle 1 (JwtAuthGuard live Account status/tokenVersion check, PortalGuard on UserProfileController, atomic compare-and-swap refresh rotation, userProfileId retained on refresh, OriginGuard on /auth/refresh, RequestContext.currentActorId() used for audit actor, dateOnlyTransformer fixing UserProfile.dateOfBirth, and removal of the fake generic PATCH /accounts/:accountId endpoint). This cycle verified each by code inspection and passing tests rather than re-implementing.\",\n    \"Fixed a genuine regression found while running test:e2e: auth-flow.e2e-spec.ts's refresh/logout tests predated the OriginGuard fix and never set an Origin header, so they failed with 403 once CORS_ORIGIN was configured. Added a `refresh()` helper that sets Origin to the first configured CORS origin, updated all refresh call sites, and added a new explicit test asserting refresh is rejected (403) with a missing or disallowed Origin and still succeeds afterwards with the allowed one.\",\n    \"Killed a stray leftover `dist/apps/worker/main` process (PID 68449, from a prior interrupted implementation attempt) that was holding port 9464 and causing media-upload-flow.e2e-spec.ts to fail with EADDRINUSE; unrelated to this cycle's code changes.\",\n    \"Interpreted AC30 (\\\"Account CRUD API hoạt động\\\") as satisfied without a generic `PATCH /accounts/:accountId` route: Account's domain model has no updatable fields beyond status/phone/password (task.md §2 explicitly excludes profile data), each of which already has its own dedicated, permission-scoped endpoint. The route list in task.md §16 is presented as a proposal (\\\"Route đề xuất\\\"), and task.md explicitly forbids updating password/phone through a generic update DTO, leaving nothing for a generic PATCH to legitimately do.\",\n    \"Per requirement-addendum.md cycle 1 (backend-only), treated AC10/AC11 (portal-specific login) as fully satisfied by backend E2E coverage of POST /auth/login with portal=PUBLIC/ADMIN, since no frontend exists in scope to originate the request. AC19 (access token kept in memory) is a frontend storage concern with no frontend in scope; the backend does not persist or dictate client-side storage, so it is treated as not applicable to this cycle rather than failed.\",\n    \"Verified (not re-implemented) that Account creation's transaction genuinely spans the identity-access/user-profiles module boundary: both modules' TypeORM repositories resolve their active connection through the same AsyncLocalStorage-backed TypeOrmQueryRunnerContext, so UserProfileProvisioner.provision() participates in CreateAccountUseCase's single UnitOfWork.withTransaction (AC29).\"\n  ],\n  \"validation\": [\n    \"backend: npm run lint -> pass\",\n    \"backend: npm run typecheck -> pass\",\n    \"backend: npm test -> pass (51 suites, 232 tests)\",\n    \"backend: npm run build -> pass\",\n    \"backend: npm run test:architecture -> pass (0 violations, 382 modules)\",\n    \"backend: npm run migration:run against a fresh empty database (memories_migration_check) -> all 5 migrations applied successfully\",\n    \"backend: npm run migration:revert x2 against the same empty database -> both new migrations (CreateUserProfilesSchema, CreateIdentityAccessSchema) reverted cleanly; temp database dropped afterward\",\n    \"backend: npm run test:e2e against docker-compose test stack (postgres/redis/minio) -> pass (4 suites, 35 tests) after fixing OriginGuard test gap and clearing a stray leftover worker process\",\n    \"backend: npm run export:openapi -> generated openapi.json with all /auth, /accounts and /user-profiles routes documented (gitignored artifact)\",\n    \"backend skill script: check_port_bindings.py -> PASSED (28 injected Symbol tokens)\",\n    \"backend skill script: check_module_wiring.py -> PASSED (27 use-case/controller classes)\",\n    \"backend skill script: check_auth_invariants.py -> PASSED\"\n  ],\n  \"current_slice\": null,\n  \"current_step\": \"All slices verified complete; wrote final implementation.json handoff\",\n  \"remaining_steps\": [],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"This attempt (cycle 2, attempt 2) found the worktree already contained a substantial, well-documented fix for all 9 items in fix-request-review-1.md, carried over from implementation cycle 1's later attempts (per .ai/metrics/agent-attempts.jsonl, attempts 4-5 of cycle 1 ran ~1400s/~1080s before the requirement change reset to cycle 2). Cycle-2 attempt 1 was very short (112s) and made no code changes.\",\n    \"The only code change made in this attempt is test-only: apps/api/test/auth-flow.e2e-spec.ts (Origin header on refresh calls + one new origin-protection test). No production source file was modified.\",\n    \"review-vertical-slice-completeness is a review-phase skill (owned by the reviewer agent per context.lock.json) and was not run by the implementer; its locked hash is not included in applied_skills below.\"\n  ]\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_token