tal=PUBLIC/ADMIN, and AC19 (access token kept in memory) as not applicable to this cycle.\",\n      \"reason\": \"requirement-addendum.md cycle 1 made MEMORIES-0002 backend-only; there is no frontend in scope to originate a 'web' login request or to choose where to store the access token. The backend enforces everything it controls (portal mapping, token issuance) and imposes no constraint against in-memory storage; the storage choice itself is a frontend concern out of scope.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The docker-compose test infrastructure containers (memories-test-postgres on :15432, memories-test-redis on :16379, memories-test-minio on :19000) referenced by .env were already running and owned by the user's environment, not started or stopped by this implementation run.\",\n    \"AC13 ('Account phải có portal.public.access để đăng nhập public nếu hệ thống áp dụng kiểm soát explicit cho public portal') is satisfied because this system does apply explicit portal control uniformly (PORTAL_PERMISSION maps both PUBLIC and ADMIN through the same permission check in LoginUseCase) -- there is no implicit-allow path for PUBLIC.\"\n  ],\n  \"validation_commands\": [\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"npm run lint\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"npm run typecheck\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"npm test\", \"result\": \"pass (51 suites, 232 tests)\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"npm run build\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"npm run test:architecture\", \"result\": \"pass (0 violations, 382 modules, 1300 dependencies)\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"DATABASE_NAME=memories_migration_check npm run migration:run (fresh empty database)\", \"result\": \"pass (all 5 migrations applied)\" },\n    { \"repo\": \"backend\", \"command\": \"DATABASE_NAME=memories_migration_check npm run migration:revert (x2